dressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUJIMOTO CHIEKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IWAI KUMIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKATANI AKIRA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SERI SHIGEMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMMURA TOSHIYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANAKA AKIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WASHINO KOMEI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJIMOTO, CHIEKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IWAI, KUMIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKATANI, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SERI, SHIGEMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMMURA, TOSHIYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, AKIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WASHINO, KOMEI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Drugs for therapeutic use characterized by containing a compound which carries in its structure at least one member selected from among -&lt;17&gt;OH, -&lt;14&gt;NH and -&lt;33&gt;SH, wherein the above &lt;17&gt;O, &lt;14&gt;N or &lt;33&gt;S exerts a relaxation effect on the proton bonded thereto and the relaxation effect is transported through the exchange of a proton in a vital component of a target organ or tissue by the above-mentioned proton, thus enabling detection by nuclear magnetic resonance. The effective circulation or distribution of such a physiologically acceptable therapeutic drug in the target organ or tissue in vivo where it is needed can be externally detected by the nuclear magnetic resonance method before the administration of a remedy to each patient or simultaneously therewith.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne des médicaments à vocation thérapeutique contenant un composé qui porte dans sa structure au moins un élément choisi parmi les -&lt;17&gt;OH, -&lt;14&gt;NH et -&lt;33&gt;SH. En l'occurrence, les &lt;17&gt;O, &lt;14&gt;N ou &lt;33&gt;S ci-dessus exercent un effet de relaxation sur le proton qui y est lié, lequel effet de relaxation se propage par l'échange d'un proton dans un composant vital d'un organe ou tissu cible avec le proton déjà mentionné, ce qui permet la détection par RMN. La circulation ou la distribution d'un tel médicament thérapeutique physiologiquement acceptable in vivo dans l'organe ou le tissu cible peut être détectée par RMN avant l'administration d'un remède à chaque patient, ou simultanément à cette administration.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://